here really is an issue of racial  equity here we all think about flint  um and the conversation about the lead  in the water there  but flint is a story that is not unique  to one particularly bad place or what's  happening in jackson is not unique to  one particular city  this is something that's playing out for  millions of americans across the country  with about 20 seconds how will president  biden's infrastructure plan  impact what we're seeing so they're  still working out the hyper-specific  details but one thing that's important  is that what president biden is  proposing  is in fact a generational investment in  infrastructure again  infrastructure's not particularly sexy  and so folks don't get as excited  necessarily as they might for something  else but that said he's  aiming to spend an amount of money if he  can get it through congress  that really is is unprecedented in our  modern history in terms of the  infrastructure the skeleton  of our country and so it's going to be  really interesting to see if that's  something he can get through washington  um and how that might change things at  communities like jackson  wesley lowry we thank you looking  forward to that report and you can watch  wesley's full report on 60 minutes plus  this sunday  on the viacom cbs streaming service  paramount plus
 

